Dan Wilson and Russ Davis each had three RBIs as Seattle opened a two-game lead over second-place California in the AL West.
"When you have a big lead, you feel a little more comfortable that you can make the pitch you want to make instead of the pitch you have to make," Johnson (14-2) said.
Johnson altered his style a bit as the result of throwing a season-high 154 pitches in his previous start, in which he fanned 16 in a 5-4 win over Kansas City on July 18.
"I got an extra day's rest and my back and my arm responded pretty well," he said. "Throwing 154 pitches is not something I want to do every day."
